Package: serie
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, git
Description: terminal UI that draws a rich git commit graph
 Serie is a terminal user interface for browsing the history of a Git
 repository. It renders the commit graph the way "git log --graph --all"
 does, but as real images drawn with the terminal emulator's image display
 protocol (Kitty or iTerm2), so branches and merges are readable at a glance
 instead of being approximated with ASCII art.
 .
 Run "serie" inside a Git repository to get a scrollable, searchable commit
 list next to the graph, with a detail view for each commit showing its
 message, refs and diff. It is a viewer, not a Git client: it does not commit,
 branch or push.
 .
 A terminal emulator supporting the Kitty or iTerm2 inline image protocol
 (for example Kitty, WezTerm, iTerm2 or Ghostty) is required for the graph to
 render.
